            "review_title": "Review at Pizza Home",
            "review_text": "Cassie W\nWindaroo, Australia862 contributions\n0\nA nice surprise for lunch\nDec 2015 • Family\nIt was one of those days where the 11 year old flat out refuses to eat at the cafe that you chose because he hasn't had western food in days and he can see a \"pizza\" sign next door. Since the pizza place looked like a tiny little hole in the wall with photos of pizzas in a book I really was not holding my breath on this one.\n\nWe pointed to a Hawaiian pizza and paid and then she led us around the back and up some very narrow stairs to an upstairs room with murals on the wall and low tables and cushions, where we waited for our meal.\n\nWhen the pizza arrived she had actually made us two pizzas. The second was some kind of sausage and capsicum. It was actually delicious and very fresh. Sometimes looks are deceiving.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 15, 2016",
